    "media:imagetext": "ANSETT\nANA\nANSETT-AN A AIRLINES OF AUSTRALIA\nTHE SYSTEM OF THE GOLDEN JETS\nELECTRA MARK 1I\nLockheed Electra Mark Il is the world's\nfastest, smoothest, quietest prop-jet airliner. Cruising\nat over 405 m.p.h., the Electra Mark I flies\nfrom Melbourne to Perth in only 43 hours.\nIts operating height of 25,000 feet avoids most\nweather turbulence, ensuring smooth, uneventful flights.\nSpecifications\nLength overall\nWing span\nTop of vertical fin from\nground\nHorizontal stabiliser width\nNormal passenger load\nWeather radar equipment\nOperating range\nwith a reserve of\n4 Allison 501-D13 turbine\nengines producing\n104 ft.\n99ft.\n32 ft. 9 ins.\n42 ft. 10 ins.\n87\n150 mile\nrange\n2,300 miles\n1,000 miles\n3,750 S.H.P.\nA MEMBER COMPANY OF ANSETT TRANSPORT INDUSTRIES LIMITED\n200/\n,106\n• 062",
